# POST-ENT — Enterprise Foundation Runtime Hardening

Durable lock: `docs/architecture/post-enterprise-foundation-runtime-hardening-governance.md`.
Enforced by `foundation:runtime-hardening-check --strict` (+ `foundation:ent-1-4-audit-check`,
`foundation:queue-worker-runtime-check`).

- This is a **post-closure hardening sprint, NOT ENT-17**. ENT-16 already closed
  ENT-1..ENT-16 with the final tag `enterprise-foundation-go`. Never move an ENT
  GO tag or the closure tag; `next_recommended_sprint` stays **MON-1**.
- **ENT-1..ENT-4** are governance/config/docs **locks** — audited (completed +
  GO-tagged + doc-backed), never retrofitted into runtime modules.
- **Queue worker**: conservative single-process systemd unit
  (`daengtisiams-queue-worker.service`), `queue:work` only (never `queue:listen`/
  `--daemon`), ENT-5 tries/backoff/timeout, broker connection (never `sync`),
  approved queues ⊆ ENT-5. The deploy script NEVER starts the worker — operator
  activates it after green gates (`queue-worker-activation-runbook.md`).
- **Deploy evidence timeout**: run the long deploy+evidence phase through
  `scripts/deploy-vps-runner.sh` (setsid/nohup + log + status file) so a dropped
  SSH pipe cannot tear down or falsely pass a deploy. GO only on `exit=0`.
- Deploy safety preserved: backup-first, `migrate --force` only, ENT-8 cache
  order; never `migrate:fresh`/`db:wipe`/`schema:drop`/`migrate:reset` on VPS.
- Destructive/sensitive literals live in config only. Evidence is non-sensitive
  (no secret/credential/backup contents/environment value/KTP/NIK). The
  `enterprise_foundation_runtime_hardening_governance` summary section is
  informational, not in the blocking combined decision. Re-verifies ENT-5..16 GO.
